<title>JAPAN: Green Cross falls on indictment of ex-presidents.</title>
<headline>Green Cross falls on indictment of ex-presidents.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Green Cross Corp fell on Friday due to news on Wednesday that prosecutors had indicted three former presidents of the drug firm, traders said.</p>
<p>The share was down 20 yen at 392 yen at 0534 GMT, after briefly dipping to 389 yen. Volume was 1.339 million shares.</p>
<p>The former presidents were indicted on charges of professional negligence resulting in the death of a patient from the company's sale of HIV-tainted blood products in the 1980s.</p>
